    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The reported outcomes are mostly classifier performance and loss-landscape indicators, not direct demonstrations that forgotten knowledge can be elicited. No uncertainty estimates are stated for the aggregate scores. The paper assumes access to a labeled validation subset for calibration.",
    "rows_left_out": "Table 3 reports detailed model-, benchmark-, and method-specific scores. They are not included here because the flattened table layout makes reliable assignment of its many values to individual conditions and metrics unclear. Figure 3 feature values are also not included because the supplied text describes the patterns but gives no numerical values.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "A",
        "parts": "Forget-set accuracy near chance, retained general ability, and robustness to simple attacks: none measured."
      },
      {
        "version": "B",
        "parts": "Recovery of forgotten knowledge by fine-tuning on any relearning set."
      },
      {
        "version": "C",
        "parts": "Activation-direction ablation. No internal analysis of blocking versus deleting; the study is black-box and loss-based only."
      },
      {
        "version": "D",
        "parts": "Low-bit quantization recovery."
      },
      {
        "version": "E",
        "parts": "Recovery by rephrasing, jailbreaks, other languages or in-context information. Paraphrases are used only as classifier inputs."
      },
      {
        "version": "F",
        "parts": "Robustness of any counter-method to recovery attacks. TAR and ELM are evaluated only as detection targets."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "Table 3 per-method results (e.g., near-100 AUC for ELM/RMU on WMDP; lower for SimNPO on MUSE) are also detector performance. They bear on no version, so their omission does not matter for this phenomenon. WMDP is an original source as a benchmark only; this study is not an original source."
